            <ArticleTitle>Report of 2 Cases of Oropharyngeal Injury With the Use of Video Laryngoscopy Techniques.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1948.e1-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.joms.2016.04.008</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0278-2391(16)30108-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although the trend toward video laryngoscopy and away from direct laryngoscopy might be associated with a greater likelihood of successful intubation, appropriate training is necessary to prevent injuries. This report describes 2 instances of operator error that resulted in penetrating injury to the soft palate and presents a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Published by Elsevier Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
